        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="metals" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="Wire drawing is a process in which wire rods/wires are reduced in diameter by drawing them through cone-shaped openings of a smaller cross section, so called dies. The input usually is wire rod of diameters raging from 5.5 to 16 mm obtained from hot rolling mills in form of coils. The final diameter size of dry drawn wire is between one and two millimetres, wet drawn wire has an even smaller diameter.;&#10;UUID: 0e9b3810-2895-33cb-884b-d0528fa86e8d" includedProcesses="Includes the process steps pre-treatment of the wire rod (mechanical descaling, pickling), dry or wet drawing (usually several drafts with decreasing die sizes), in some cases heat treatment (continuous-/discontinuous annealing, patenting, oil hardening) and Finishing. Does not include coating and the material being rolled" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="metals" localName="Wire drawing, steel" localSubCategory="chipless shaping" name="Wire drawing, steel" subCategory="chipless shaping" unit="kg"/>
